# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# [LEX-2] normalises line endings inside the compiler, so a mixed-ending file
# still compiles — but scripted edits and diffs against the emitted C both go
# wrong quietly when the tree is mixed. Pin it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Owner-supplied custody artifacts are retained byte-for-byte. Their original
# line endings and trailing bytes are part of the recorded integrity hash.
docs/spec-source/as-received/** -text

*.png binary
*.pdf binary
